    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Give one reason why English continued to be used in India after Independence.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "People of the south those who could not speak Hindi, opposed Hindi as National Language. They threatened to separate from India if Hindi was imposed on them. The Constituent Assembly finally decided that Hindi would be the \"official language\" of India and English would be used in the courts, the services, and communications between one state and another.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, English continued to be used for administrative and inter-state communication.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
